a skipped path, not a path with the same prefix
JSON(SKIP a, SKIP b)
{"ab":2,"t":4}
{"ab":2,"t":4}
JSON(SKIP s)
{"t":5}
{"t":5}
a path inside a skipped one, with another skipped path sorted between them
JSON(SKIP a, SKIP `a-b`)
{"c":3}
{"c":3}
regular expressions match partially or fully by the setting
JSON(SKIP REGEXP 'b') --type_json_use_partial_match_to_skip_paths_by_regexp=1
{"c":2}
{"c":2}
JSON(SKIP REGEXP 'b') --type_json_use_partial_match_to_skip_paths_by_regexp=0
{"ab":1,"c":2}
{"ab":1,"c":2}
the limit on the number of paths of an object in binary input
TOO_LARGE_ARRAY_SIZE
